# Challenges – Sprint 29

## Challenges Faced

### Challenge 1

After successfully updating the Student Profile, the Eligible Jobs component was still displaying the old eligibility information.

### Solution

Identified that the Eligible Jobs data was stale and needed to be refreshed after the Student record was updated.

---

### Challenge 2

Understanding how the Student Profile component could inform the Eligible Jobs component that the profile had been successfully saved.

### Solution

Added a `profilesaved` Custom Event in the Student Profile component and used a common `StudentPortal` parent component to coordinate the communication.

---

### Challenge 3

Refreshing the wired eligible jobs data after the Student Profile was updated.

### Solution

Stored the wired Apex result and used `refreshApex()` through a public `refreshJobs()` method in the Eligible Jobs component.

---

### Challenge 4

Integrating the new parent component into the existing application without affecting the existing JobCard and Eligible Jobs functionality.

### Solution

Created the `StudentPortal` component as a common parent for `StudentProfile` and `EligibleJobs` and added it to the existing Lightning App Builder page.

---

### Challenge 5

Testing whether the updated student information was reflected in the Eligible Jobs component.

### Solution

Deployed the changes and updated the student's profile information. After saving the profile, the Eligible Jobs component refreshed successfully and displayed the updated eligibility information.
